//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E63 - THE 5m TIMEFRAME RESCALE. BOTH HALVES FAIL.
//   H1 2024-06-08 -> 2025-07-20  https://mcp-api.trader.dev/backtest/01M1KJMNNJV95QMD3WRVERSN9T
//        PF 0.70674847 | DD 31.81350346% | 95 trades | 29.47% win | avgBarsInTrade 225.71 / 1296
//   H2 2025-07-20 -> 2026-09-01  https://mcp-api.trader.dev/backtest/01M1KJND79NQ4WEQ4QY6H7ZCDH
//        PF 0.83434289 | DD 16.01925213% | 73 trades | 32.88% win | avgBarsInTrade 292.85 / 1296
//
// PARENT: e58a (shield $1,000, maxBars 6480) - the family's largest 1m sample at 36 trades AND
// confirmed reproducible by E59's cross-session cold re-run. E38 and E47 are unreproducible
// (HARD LESSON 25) and were not used.
//
// SCALING TABLE - only two parameters are bar counts:
//   maxBars    6480 -> 1296    (6480 x 1m and 1296 x 5m are both 4.5 days)
//   ta.atr(30) -> ta.atr(6)    (30 x 1m and 6 x 5m are both 30 minutes)
//   skipOpen / skipClose        UNCHANGED - MINUTES, from minsIn, not bars
//   greenBull 4                 UNCHANGED - a count of 1h candles
//   shieldUsd / rr / velK / midLo / midHi / etOffset  UNCHANGED - dollars and ratios
//
// WHY NOT 15m: the 15m level is reconstructed from timestamps, so on a 15m entry every bar IS one
// bucket, p15l collapses to the previous bar's low, and brokeBelow stops being a structural level.
// The entry cannot be lifted above the lowest structural rung of its own cascade.
//
// WHAT IT FOUND. The ceiling is gone - 168 trades against the 20-30 this family had been capped at
// since E35 - and the edge went with it. THE SHARPER POINT: avgBarsInTrade is 17% and 23% of the cap,
// so THE CAP DOES NOT BIND AT 5m. Every previous ALCM measurement had winners pinned at 56-93% of
// their cap. **This is the first measurement in this lab where the exit resolves at target or
// liquidation as the specification requires - and it returns 0.71 and 0.83.**
//
// THE LIKELIER READING: not that the family is 1m-specific, but that e58a's 1.24 on 36 trades was
// small-sample noise and 168 trades is the more trustworthy number. Do not retreat to the 1m window;
// results there are not more real for being more flattering.
//
// AUDIT: LONG only, no short leg since E45/E46, nothing mirrored (LESSON 6). R = $1,000, ~1-2% of
// price, clears the 0.8% floor (LESSON 3). Stop RISK-DEFINED, the DECLARED deviation the ALCM
// requires (LESSON 5). SL and TP fixed at entry. Latch order intact (HARD LESSON 8). Occupancy change
// from 5m trigger density named in advance (HARD LESSONS 24/28/29): one fifth the trigger
// opportunities, wall-clock hold preserved.
// WAR FORMATION E58a — THE SHIELD SWEPT DOWN. E57 SWEPT UP ($3,000/$4,000) AND FOUND THE SAMPLE
// COLLAPSES BELOW THE FLOOR REGARDLESS OF MAXBARS SCALING. THIS SIDE OF THE AXIS HAS NEVER BEEN RUN.
//
// HARD LESSON 23 (STRATEGY-LEDGER.md) already settled that drawdowns need no leverage rescaling and
// that risk per trade is exactly shieldUsd/price under the engine's forced 100%-of-equity, 1x-margin
// sizing -- so "position sizing / risk fraction" (E57's queue item 1) is NOT a separate lever from
// shieldUsd. It is the same lever the shield sweep already varies. The one direction of that lever
// E38-41/E47/E48/E57 never tried is DOWN from $2,000. This file is that test.
//
// DECLARED DEVIATION FROM ORACLE-RULES.md: the source material names $3,000 ("$4,000 is safer") as
// the shield, not $1,000. $2,000 was already an off-spec working anchor, kept "by elimination, not
// because it beat the wider shields on their merits" (E57's own words) -- this file moves further off
// spec, in the direction of MORE testability, not less, purely to find out whether the shieldUsd axis
// is informative about the edge at all on this 4.5-month window before the lab spends more credits on
// widths ORACLE-RULES actually asks for but this data cannot measure.
//
// MAXBARS SCALING: E57 found hold time scales SUPER-linearly with R going up (77%/97% of a linearly
// projected cap, not ~56%). Going down, the mechanism should point the other way: rr is unchanged
// (2.0), so a smaller shieldUsd also means a proportionally NEARER target (tpPx = close + shieldUsd*rr)
// -- less distance to travel, not more -- so linear-or-tighter scaling is the conservative (unlikely to
// truncate) assumption here, unlike the upward sweep. maxBars scaled linearly from e50b's anchor:
// 12960 * (1000/2000) = 6480. Stated as an assumption, not a verified law, exactly as E57's was.
//
// THE SPECIFICATION: War Formation has NO STOP LOSS. The exit is the A.L.C.M. shield -- a fixed dollar
// gap to liquidation. The position ends at target or at liquidation. NEVER add to a losing trade.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT:
//   LONG (only leg) -- R = shieldUsd = $1,000, ~1.0% of BTC price: PASSES the 0.8% floor (HARD LESSON
//     3), though narrower than any shield tested in this family so far -- flagged, not hidden. Stop is
//     RISK-DEFINED, not structural -- the declared ALCM deviation from HARD LESSON 5. SL/TP fixed at
//     entry, no trailing. Latch order unchanged from e50b (HARD LESSON 8). coilPrev stays removed
//     (unchanged from e50b, not this run's question).
//   SHORT -- DELETED (identical to e50a/e50b): no short entry can fire; position_size can never be
//     negative (HARD LESSON 6, trivially satisfied).
//   Redundancy (HARD LESSON 18): none introduced; byte-identical to e50b except shieldUsd and maxBars.
//
// PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOME (HARD LESSON 17), against e50b's PF 1.21869905 / 21 trades / avgBarsWinning
// 56.5% at $2,000/12960:
//   - PF stays clearly above 1.0 AND trade count rises meaningfully above 21 -> a narrower shield both
//     buys sample AND does not cost edge -- the most promising direction this axis has produced, though
//     still off-spec and needing E58b (the $1,500 sibling) before either is trusted (HARD LESSON 16).
//   - PF collapses even with an adequate (>=20) trade count -> a nearer target genuinely hurts this
//     construction's edge, independent of sample size -- consistent with E26's finding that a nearer
//     target hurt the (unrelated) short construction, now tested on the long leg.
//   - Trade count still fails to clear ~20 despite the smaller R -> the occupancy/latch mechanics (not
//     R itself) are what caps this construction's sample on this window, and the shieldUsd axis is not
//     informative in either direction on 4.5 months of 1m data -- closes "position sizing/risk fraction"
//     as unproductive here, same as the upward sweep closed for the opposite reason.
//
// SAMPLE CEILING: ~3 days per trade across 4.5 months of 1m data (2025-12-16 to 2026-05-03) caps this
// family near 20-30 trades under the anchor's own hold-time profile; a narrower shield may resolve
// faster and lift that ceiling, which is exactly what this run tests. A ratio below ~20 trades is
// reported as a COUNT, not read as a result.
strategy("E63 5m rescale War Formation E58a shield1000 cap6480", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

greenBull = input.int(4,     "Green 1h candles for BULL")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min reclaim as multiple of atr(30)")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
etOffset  = input.int(-4,    "ET offset from UTC")
witchOn   = input.bool(true, "Ban longs in witching hour 1-4am ET")
shieldUsd = input.float(1000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation")
rr        = input.float(2.0, "Reward:risk")
maxBars   = input.int(1296,  "Max bars in trade -- 6480/5, same 4.5 days of wall clock")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000
MS15 = 900000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)
b15 = math.floor(time / MS15)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]
new15 = b15 != b15[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   grnCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   grnPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

if new6
    grnPrev := grnCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    grnCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] > h1o
            grnCur := grnCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bullRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev >= greenBull

minsIn    = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate  = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

h1Bull = not na(h1o) and close > h1o

var float c15l = na
var float p15l = na

if new15
    p15l := c15l
    c15l := low
else
    c15l := na(c15l) ? low : math.min(c15l, low)

brokeBelow = not na(p15l) and c15l < p15l

velMin = na(ta.atr(6)) ? na : ta.atr(6) * velK   // 30/5, same 30 minutes

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

hUTC     = math.floor(time / MS1H) % 24
hET      = (hUTC + etOffset + 24) % 24
witching = hET >= 1 and hET < 4
longBan  = witchOn and witching

longTrig  = not na(p15l) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossover(close, p15l) and (close - p15l) >= velMin

goLong  = bullRegime and timeGate and h1Bull and brokeBelow and not inMiddle and not longBan and longTrig

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

longR = shieldUsd

if flat and goLong and longR > 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := close - longR
    tpPx   := close + longR * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
